{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Why do you ask for my name?</b> He said: you have no benefit from knowing my name, for the power and the ability belong to YHWH alone — if you call me I will not answer you, nor will I deliver you from your trouble; but now I will bless you, for so I have been commanded. And Scripture did not specify the blessing, and the most likely explanation is what our Rabbis said (in Midrash Aggadah and in Zohar, Toldot 144a), that he acknowledged to him all the blessings there in that place under compulsion, for Jacob did not wish to wait for him until Bethel."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:42.800611296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}